      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plano%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Plano Manufacturing Company, later known as the Plano Harvester Company, powered the town’s growth from the 1860s through the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plano%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Plano’s Plano Molding Company still manufactures fishing tackle and plastic containers, keeping the town’s industrial roots alive today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plano%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2011, downtown Plano doubled as the fictional Smallville in the Superman film, Man of Steel, drawing Hollywood to the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        17,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plano%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Plano Harvester’s reaper mascot inspired Plano High School’s sports teams, a nod to the town’s agricultural heritage.",
